  "nothing_here_is_evidence_about_RH": true,
  "question": "bipartite S-unit difference pattern for Erdos #126",
  "reduction": {
    "conditional": "If log N2(k) = o(k) then Erdos #126 holds. The known lower bounds on S-unit-equation solution counts (Erdos-Stewart-Tijdeman 1988; Konyagin-Soundararajan 2007, exp(k^(2-sqrt2-o(1)))) are all exp(k^theta) with theta < 1, so log N2(k) = o(k) is consistent with everything known and is the expected truth. Sufficient, not necessary: the reduction is measurably lossy.",
    "explicit_corollary": {
      "bound_on_f": "f(n) > k whenever n > 2 + 3*7^(2k+3); i.e. f(n) >= (log(n-2) - log 3)/(2 log 7) - 3/2",
      "bound_on_g": "g(k) <= 3 * 7^(2k+3) + 2",
      "input": "Evertse 1984, Invent. Math. 75: alpha*x + beta*y = 1 in S-units of a degree-d field with s places has at most 3 * 7^(d + 2s) solutions; here d = 1, s = k + 1.",
      "log_slope": 3.8918202981106265
    },
    "improvement_from_within_part_structure": "None in the exponent. The extra sums buy a free nondegeneracy guarantee for the 4-term relation (a+b)+(c+d)=(a+c)+(b+d), but routing through it needs 3-term unit equations whose best uniform bound exp((6n)^(3n)(r+1)) with n=3 is exp(~2e11 * k), vastly worse than 7^(2k).",
    "proof_sketch": "Fix a1 != a2 in A, c = a1 - a2. For every other x in A the pair (u,v) = (x+a1, x+a2) consists of S-units with u - v = c, and x is recovered as u - a1, so the map is injective.",
    "statement": "g(k) <= N2(k) + 2, where N2(k) = max over |S|=k and c in Q* of #{(u,v) in (Z_S^*)^2 : u - v = c}.",
    "uses_only_pattern": "K_{2,m} (two anchors joined to m vertices)"
  }
}